ell_vee for the sharp cut-off: ln(1-a) vs numerical:
   a=k+/vee=1e-01:  ln(1-a)=-1.053605e-01   -int_0^a dxi/(1-xi) = -1.053605e-01
   a=k+/vee=1e-02:  ln(1-a)=-1.005034e-02   -int_0^a dxi/(1-xi) = -1.005034e-02
   a=k+/vee=1e-03:  ln(1-a)=-1.000500e-03   -int_0^a dxi/(1-xi) = -1.000500e-03

smooth cut-offs: ell_f(a)/a  (-> -kappa_f) ;  kappa_f
   sharp     : ell_f/a at a=1e-2,1e-3,1e-4: -1.00503 -1.00050 -1.00005   kappa_f =  1.00000
   exp(-u^2) : ell_f/a at a=1e-2,1e-3,1e-4: -2.18207 -1.81588 -1.77697   kappa_f =  1.77245
   1/(1+u^2) : ell_f/a at a=1e-2,1e-3,1e-4: -1.97824 -1.61401 -1.57529   kappa_f =  1.57080
   (for f with f'(0) != 0, e.g. exp(-u), also the observed gluon itself gets the weight f(k+/vee) = 1 - O(k+/vee),
    which multiplies L as well: ell_f ~ -a [ln(k+/Lambda) + O(1)], again O(k+/vee) times logarithms; not shown.)

   eps=1e-01: a=1e-2,1e-4,1e-6 ->  1.005e-01  1.000e-03  1.000e-05
   eps=1e-02: a=1e-2,1e-4,1e-6 ->  1.005e+00  1.000e-02  1.000e-04
   eps=1e-03: a=1e-2,1e-4,1e-6 ->  1.005e+01  1.000e-01  1.000e-03
   vee->oo at fixed eps: 0;  eps->0 at fixed vee: diverges.  At leading power in a = k+/vee the term is absent.
